#import(../../prelude/num.gill)

% contention.gill — TODO_0284 PT: the executable separation witness (E1)
% between the two side-conditions of the settle-optimality theorem
% (doc/paper/settle-optimality.md §3):
%
%   choice-freedom      (tied instances independent)     ⟹  T1 confluence
%   contention-freedom  (ALL enabled instances independent) ⟹ T2 σ*-optimality
%
% and choice-freedom does NOT imply contention-freedom. Program E1:
% r1 and r2 compete for the one `tok`, but at DIFFERENT activations
% (0 vs 5) — they are never tied, so the run is deterministic and
% trivially confluent (T1 holds, the PRF chooser is never consulted).
% Yet the monotone relaxation (facts as reusable values, Dyna-style)
% derives won_b@5; the linear run fires r1 at the frontier 0, consumes tok,
% and r2 is starved FOREVER. σ* is not realized: T2's hypothesis is
% violated and its conclusion genuinely fails.
%
% The m-program is the same shape with the token READ instead of
% consumed — contention-free by construction (reads disable nothing) —
% and the relaxation stamp won_b2@5 IS realized: exactly the Dyna/monotone
% recovery of §4.
%
% E2 (the deferred-producer twin, §3 "why the relaxation"): b3 is not
% initial — mk3 produces it at 5. Every run-reachable E(s) is a SINGLETON
% (e1/e2 are never co-enabled), so a contention condition quantified over
% run states holds vacuously — yet tok3 is spent at 0 and won_b3@5 is
% starved exactly as in E1. The demand overlap between e1 and e2 exists
% only in the monotone relaxation; contention-freedom must be read there.

tok: type.
a: type.
b: type.
won_a: type.
won_b: type.

rtok: type.
a2: type.
b2: type.
won_a2: type.
won_b2: type.

tok3: type.
a3: type.
b3: type.
c3: type.
won_a3: type.
won_b3: type.

% E1: one token, two consumers at different activations.
r1: a * tok -o { won_a }.
r2: b * tok -o { won_b }.

% E1 relaxed: the token is read, not consumed.
m1: a2 * read rtok -o { won_a2 }.
m2: b2 * read rtok -o { won_b2 }.

% E2: as E1, but the competitor's enabling token is produced mid-run.
e1: a3 * tok3 -o { won_a3 }.
e2: b3 * tok3 -o { won_b3 }.
mk3: c3 -o { b3 }.

% The committed world: r1 fires at 0 (the frontier), won_a@0; b survives
% untouched at 5.
#expect_committed (settle: 10)
  a * tok * b@5
  =>
  won_a * b@5 .

% The starved derivation: won_b@5 is derivable in the monotone relaxation
% (σ*(won_b) = 5 ⊑ horizon) but NOT reachable — r1's firing consumed tok
% before r2's activation arrived. Deterministic, confluent, suboptimal.
#expect_not_starved (settle: 10)
  a * tok * b@5
  =>
  won_b@5 .

% The contention-free twin realizes BOTH relaxation stamps: won_a2 at 0,
% won_b2 at max(5, 0) = 5 — the read stamp joins the activation, nothing
% is disabled, settle ≡ the monotone least fixed point (T2).
#expect_recovery (settle: 10)
  a2 * rtok * b2@5
  =>
  won_a2 * won_b2@5 .

% E2 committed world: e1 fires at 0 (the only enabled instance — E(s) is
% a singleton at every reachable state); mk3 fires at 5; b3 survives.
#expect_committed_deferred (settle: 10)
  a3 * tok3 * c3@5
  =>
  won_a3 * b3@5 .

% E2 starvation: σ*(won_b3) = 5 in the relaxation, never realized — and no
% run state ever exhibits the contention (e1 and e2 are never co-enabled).
#expect_not_starved_deferred (settle: 10)
  a3 * tok3 * c3@5
  =>
  won_b3@5 .
